## Multi-tenancy rule
Every database query that touches business data **must** filter by `businessId`. Never return cross-tenant data. The `businessId` is always derived from the authenticated user — never from a request body or query param.

## Roles
`SUPER_ADMIN` · `BUSINESS_ADMIN` · `STAFF` — defined in `UserRole` Prisma enum. UI gated via `/me/ui` endpoint.

## Auth flow
JWT access token (short-lived) + refresh token stored in `RefreshToken` table with indexed `tokenPrefix` (first 8 chars) for O(1) lookup. **Signup:** WhatsApp OTP → set password. **Login:** mobile + password. **Forgot password:** `/forgot-password` via OTP. Dev OTP bypass: `1234`; dev code shown in signup UI when WA not connected. Empty `JWT_SECRET` falls back to `dev` locally. Global rate limit: 60 req/min via `ThrottlerModule`; auth routes 10/min.

## Dynamic content (SiteContent)
All user-facing text (landing page, SEO metadata, WhatsApp message templates, city pages, onboarding text) is stored in the `SiteContent` model. Keys use dotted namespaces: `landing.hero.title`, `seo.landing.description`, `wa.booking_confirm`. Editable by Super Admin at `/app/superadmin/content`. Redis cached for 5 minutes — invalidated on update.

## WhatsApp automation (BullMQ)
- `booking_confirm` — enqueued immediately when appointment status → CONFIRMED
- `reminder_24h` — enqueued at appointment creation, delayed to `startAt − 24h`
- `post_visit` — enqueued when status → COMPLETED, delayed 24h
- `inactive_recovery` — scaffolded; requires a cron to trigger
- All message templates are fetched from `SiteContent` DB at job processing time (supports Super Admin edits without redeploy)

## Redis / graceful degradation
- `REDIS_URL` in production currently points to localhost (placeholder) — slot lock and BullMQ degrade gracefully
- Slot lock: if Redis is unavailable `redisAvailable=false` → skips lock, proceeds with Prisma TX only
- SiteContent caching: try/catch around all Redis ops → falls back to DB query
- BullMQ queue `add()` calls: all wrapped in try/catch → non-fatal, reminders skipped if Redis down

## Key files
- `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma` — source of truth for all data models
- `apps/api/src/common/` — guards, decorators, tenant helpers
- `apps/api/src/site-content/` — dynamic content module (public GET, super-admin PUT, Redis cache)
- `apps/api/src/worker.ts` — BullMQ job processor (run separately from API)
- `apps/api/src/queues/queues.module.ts` — REDIS + QUEUE_WHATSAPP + QUEUE_REMINDERS providers
- `apps/web/src/app/` — Next.js App Router routes
- `apps/web/src/lib/site-content.ts` — client helpers for fetching SiteContent from API (ISR revalidate 300s)
- `apps/web/messages/en.json` + `messages/hi.json` — static UI strings for next-intl
- `apps/web/src/i18n/request.ts` — next-intl locale resolution from `locale` cookie
- `apps/web/src/components/lang-switcher.tsx` — EN ↔ HI toggle component
- `PLANS.md` — current dev status and next steps

## SEO conventions
- All Next.js pages that are server components export `generateMetadata()` pulling from `getSiteContentGroup("seo")`
- `[slug]/page.tsx` is a server wrapper around `booking-client.tsx` — adds metadata + JSON-LD `LocalBusiness` schema
- `apps/web/src/app/sitemap.ts` — static routes + city pages
- `apps/web/src/app/robots.ts` — allow public, disallow `/app/`, `/api/`

## Design principles
- Mobile-first; tap targets ≥ 44px; bottom nav for primary actions
- Emerald + Zinc palette; glassmorphism subtle; motion ≤ 200ms
- No ERP vocabulary; no dense tables on mobile; Hub is the default home
- Date always on first line, time on second line (Hub "Leads & tickets" pattern)
- `StatCard`, `Card`, `Button`, `FormField`, `FieldInput` are shared UI components in `@/components/ui`

## Money / numbers
- All prices stored as integer cents (`priceCents`, `amountCents`)
- Display: `₹${Math.round(cents / 100).toLocaleString("en-IN")}`
- Never store or compute with floats for money
